; take/drop must use SRFI-1 argument order: (take lst n) / (drop lst n).
; The VM's embedded prelude used to define them reversed as (take n lst) /
; (drop n lst), diverging from core/list/transform.esk (the on-disk stdlib
; module the native/AOT compiler uses). A list and a distinct-type numeric
; count make a reversed order fail LOUDLY (a type error trying to treat the
; list as a count, or the count as a list) instead of silently returning the
; wrong value.
(display (take '(a b c d e) 3)) (newline)
(display (drop '(a b c d e) 3)) (newline)
(display (take (list 10 20 30 40) 0)) (newline)
(display (drop (list 10 20 30 40) 4)) (newline)
(display (take '(1 2 3) 5)) (newline)
(display (drop '(1 2 3) 5)) (newline)
